__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
# Without the trailing slash too: a pattern ending in `/` matches only a
# DIRECTORY, so a `.venv` SYMLINK to one slips past `.venv/` and can be
# committed. That happened on PR #26 — a 120000 blob holding an absolute
# path on one machine, which is a dangling link for every other clone.
.venv
venv
.DS_Store
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Coverage outputs — `pytest --cov` writes these; locally they're throwaway.
.coverage
coverage.json
htmlcov/
# Runtime profile individuation from `agentctl spawn` / `co` dispatch into this repo
.claude/
# Vault data never belongs in the repo: the Chart House and the Archives are
# databases on the mini with their own backups (ADR-0022). A stray .db here is a
# copy of live lock state in git history.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Shadow comparison series. `shadow.py --series` records what the two services
# answered, so a run against live traffic writes real row ids and real
# disagreements. Field values from customer-class rows are redacted before they
# are written, and this is the second line rather than the first: a plaintext
# artifact of a live read surface does not belong in git whatever it holds.
#
# Matched by the documented artifact name rather than by `*.jsonl`, which would
# silently untrack any future JSONL fixture anywhere in the repo (reviewer,
# PR #3). A series written somewhere else is not covered, so the redaction above
# is what actually protects the content.
shadow-series*

# Runtime logs from serve.sh / shadow.py — machine state, never the repo's.
serve.log
shadow-run.log
.uvicorn.log

# Swift Package Manager build output for root-ca.
root-ca/.build/
root-ca/.swiftpm/
